Wire speech synthesis, notifications and media sessions to HarmonyOS.

Absorbs, in this order: ohos-tts.patch, ohos-notifications.patch, ohos-media-session.patch. Their descriptions follow.

--- ohos-tts.patch

Speak with HarmonyOS CoreSpeechKit.

speech/tts_ohos.cc (overlay) now talks to the engine HAR's TtsService over
//components/ohos_system_service instead of reporting TTS as unsupported.

--- ohos-notifications.patch

Show web notifications as HarmonyOS notifications.

notification_platform_bridge_ohos.cc (overlay) now publishes through the
engine HAR's NotificationService over //components/ohos_system_service instead
of returning the stub bridge, which showed nothing.

--- ohos-media-session.patch

Publish the page's media session to HarmonyOS AVSession.

The control center and lock screen show what a page is playing and send play,
pause, next, previous, stop and seek back to it. The implementation is
components/system_media_controls/ohos/ (overlay), on the OH_AVSession C API.

kHardwareMediaKeyHandling is what makes the browser create system media
controls at all, so it is enabled on OHOS. OHOS has no ui::MediaKeysListener
(the stub returns null), so if AVSession cannot be created the manager stays
without either instead of dereferencing a null listener.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.
Apply with:

  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-system-services.patch

